# Proxy routing requests to the OpenTripPlanner instance (Monash / ARDC Nectar).
#
# This MUST stay above the SPA catch-all below. If /* comes first it swallows /otp/*,
# and every routing request returns index.html instead of a result — which looks exactly
# like the routing server being down.
#
# The 200 status makes this a proxy rather than a redirect: Netlify fetches the routing
# service server-side and returns the result as if it came from this domain. That is what
# lets an HTTPS page reach an HTTP routing service without the browser blocking it as
# mixed content.
#
# If the routing server moves, change the address here and redeploy. No code change.
/otp/*    http://203.101.230.213:8080/otp/:splat    200
/gtfs-rt/rapid-bus-kl https://api.data.gov.my/gtfs-realtime/vehicle-position/prasarana/?category=rapid-bus-kl 200
/api/reliability/* https://transitreach-reliability-api.onrender.com/api/reliability/:splat 200

# SPA fallback — must remain last.
/*        /index.html                               200
